<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Province of Hesse-Nassau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Province of Hesse-Nassau was a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> formed in 1868 from lands annexed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866: the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, the Duchy of Nassau and the Free City of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>. Its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>. Waldeck was added in 1929. It was divided in 1944, and most of it is now in the German state of Hesse.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/province-of-hesse-nassau.jpg" alt="Province of Hesse-Nassau" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flagge_Preu%C3%9Fen_-_Provinz_Hessen-Nassau.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
